 238  4203              ; show: the pairs' patterns at the scroll's shift, NB bytes after the paper
 239  4203              ; (chapter 29), each shift in a page of its own: the page is high shifts plus
 240  4203              ; the shift, and no multiplication. The NB bytes go by NB OUTIs one after
 241  4203              ; another, 18 T-states a byte: the border takes them as fast as that (chapter
 242  4203              ; 20). And when the scroll has reached a new column, the table that holds it
 243  4203              ; shown with R#2, and the next window to be written
